= Editing and publishing the website

== Content and layout

The website is generated by Typst 0.15.1. There is no intermediate Markdown,
hand-maintained HTML, or JavaScript rendering application. The compiler creates
all page markup from Typst; the browser applies the CSS in `assets/site.css`.

- `content/`: French page sources. Ordinary paragraphs, headings, lists and links
  use Typst markup.
- `site.typ`: the site name, contact address and navigation.
- `theme.typ`: the HTML structure, page template and reusable content functions.
- `assets/`: local photographs, diagrams and CSS.
- `main.typ`: the list of pages emitted by Typst’s bundle exporter.
- `dist/`: generated deployment files, ignored by Git.

Each page begins with an import of the shared theme and a page show rule. Edit
the content below those lines. A heading beginning with `==` becomes a section
heading; the page template already supplies the main heading.

```typst
#import "/theme.typ": *
#show: page.with(title: "La Société", path: "la-societe/")

Une nouvelle description de notre association.

== Nos activités

- Navigation à la rame
- Navigation à la gaffe

#site-link("sport/cours/")[Découvrir les cours]
```

Use `site-link` for links within this website so they work beneath the GitHub
Pages repository path. Use Typst’s `link` for external URLs. Add images to
`assets/` and use `photo` with a meaningful alternative description. The theme
embeds CSS and images into the HTML, so each page is also independently viewable.

== Editing in the Typst web app

Import the repository files into a Typst project, preserving the directory
structure. Choose compiler version 0.15.1, enable the experimental HTML feature
in project settings, and choose HTML preview. Select `content/index.typ`, or the
page you are editing, as the previewed file.

The web app does not yet support bundle export. Preview the individual content
files there; GitHub Actions compiles `main.typ` as a bundle to build every page.
The site navigation uses deployment paths and is intended for the deployed site;
to switch pages in the web editor, select the corresponding source file.

Typst’s Git Sync integration requires a Pro plan. Connect this GitHub repository
in the project settings, pull before editing and push when ready. On plans
without Git Sync, export the changed project sources and commit them with Git.
Simply editing a document in Typst does not update GitHub until those changes
are pushed.

#link("https://typst.app/docs/web-app/git-sync/")[Typst Git Sync documentation]

== Local build and preview

Install the CLI release recorded in `.typst-version`, then run:

```sh
bash scripts/build.sh
python3 scripts/check.py
```

Invoke the build through Bash: browser-based editors and Git synchronization
can save shell scripts without their executable permission. The CI workflow
uses the same command, so publishing does not depend on that permission.

The build uses Typst’s native `html` and `bundle` experimental features. A failed
compile leaves the previous `dist/` intact. The compiler’s experimental-feature
warning is expected. Keep the version pin until a newer compiler has been tested.

For a live preview of the complete site:

```sh
typst watch --root . --features html,bundle --format bundle main.typ dist
```

Typst prints the local preview URL and rebuilds when a source or asset changes.
Stop it with Ctrl-C. The generated pages do not contain application JavaScript;
Typst injects a reload script only into the live preview it serves.

To reproduce the GitHub Pages subdirectory locally:

```sh
BASE_PATH=/pontonnier/ bash scripts/build.sh
python3 scripts/check.py --base-path /pontonnier/
```

A server for this build must mount `dist/` at `/pontonnier/`. Use the default
root build for Typst’s local preview server.

== Publishing

Push a commit to `main`. The GitHub Actions workflow compiles and validates the
root build, then builds for the base path returned by GitHub Pages. It checks
local links, anchors, image descriptions and the page structure before uploading
the artifact and deploying it. A pull request runs checks without deployment.

The repository’s Pages setting must use *GitHub Actions* as its build source.
Deployment uses the workflow’s short-lived GitHub token and does not require a
personal access token or a hosting password. The default site address is
#link("https://lcnbr.github.io/pontonnier/").

A custom domain is not configured. To move to one later, configure it in GitHub
Pages and update DNS; the workflow takes the new base path from Pages.

== Adding a page

Create a content file using an existing page as a starting point. Add its source
and output path to `main.typ`, and a navigation entry to `site.typ` if needed.
Run the build and validation at both root and repository paths before pushing.

== Reference scope

The main sections are reproduced as editable Typst pages. Introductory text is
adapted from the source, and the layout follows its centered Twenty Ten design.
Historical albums, detailed technical references, videos and downloadable PDFs
link to their existing locations. The Rhonomètre remains an external embed.
The static contact page opens email or telephone links; it does not run the
original WordPress contact form. The live club’s domain is not modified.
